      "pageDescription": "",
      "evidenceText": "University of Vienna Faculty of Law Fellowship Programme – Summer 2027 – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram University of Vienna Faculty of Law Fellowship Programme – Summer 2027 Jude Ogar November 5, 2026 2 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: November 30, 2026 Applications are open for the University of Vienna Faculty of Law Fellowship Programme – Summer 2027 . The programme aims to promote international academic exchange and foster collaboration between international fellows and members of the faculty. It offers both early-career and established researchers the opportunity to pursue their research in an international academic environment, benefit from the faculty’s expertise and establish new scholarly connections. Building on the faculty’s existing research initiatives and diverse research priorities, the programme seeks to encourage interdisciplinary exchange, strengthen international research networks and create opportunities for long-term academic collaboration. Fellowship For the summer semester of 2027, the Faculty of Law offers: Senior Fellowships for professors, providing financial support of EUR 1,050 per month. Junior Fellowships for doctoral and postdoctoral researchers, providing financial support of EUR 800 per month. Eligibility Applicants must be researchers affiliated with a university outside Austria and must not have been employed by the University of Vienna at any time in the last six months. Applicants must propose a research project that aligns with one or more of the Faculty of Law’s research priorities. In addition, a letter of endorsement from a university professor, a member of staff with a habilitation, an associate professor or an assistant professor at the Faculty of Law is required. This should include a brief explanation of why the applicant is particularly well-suited for the fellowship. Application A complete application must include the following documents: A completed application form . A letter of application (maximum three pages) outlining the proposed research project, its alignment with the faculty’s research priorities and the academic expertise of the proposed supervisor, as well as the applicant’s motivation for choosing the Faculty of Law at the University of Vienna as their host institution. A curriculum vitae (CV) (maximum three pages) including the five key publications for senior fellows and postdoctoral researchers; for predoctoral researchers a letter of recommendation from their supervisor. PhD students are additionally required to submit a letter of recommendation from their current supervisor at their home university. A supervision agreement from the Faculty of Law at the University of Vienna. Applications may be submitted to [email protected] from 1 November 2026 to 30 November 2026 (inclusive). Selection decisions will be made in December 2026. For more information, visit University of Vienna Fellowship . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article 21 Hot Job Opportunities Currently Open – November 5, 2026 Next Article How to Ace Your Scholarship Interview: 12 Tips to Help You Stand Out Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 3 days Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 80 days Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 21 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
