      "pageTitle": "IX-WAI Early Career Development Grant 2027 (up to £1,000) &#8211; Opportunity Desk",
      "pageDescription": "",
      "evidenceText": "IX-WAI Early Career Development Grant 2027 (up to £1,000) – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram IX-WAI Early Career Development Grant 2027 (up to £1,000) Jude Ogar November 5, 2026 3 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: January 4, 2027 Applications are open for the IX-WAI Early Career Development Grant 2027 . The I-X Women in AI Network (IX-WAI) provides Early Career Development Grants of up to £1,000 to women and non-binary individuals who are currently working in AI or wish to enter the field. These grants are intended to support conference attendance, workshops, training, and other professional development opportunities. This initiative reflects the commitment to providing additional support for women and non-binary individuals in AI. Grant The grant can cover registration fees and travel expenses for conferences, workshops, tutorials, training sessions, and other activities that enable applicants to present their research, expand their professional networks, and develop new skills in AI. Eligibility Open to women and non-binary individuals at Master’s, PhD, or postdoctoral level at Imperial College London who are interested in learning about AI or are currently working in the field. Applicants who have already been awarded this grant are not eligible to apply again. Selection Criteria The proposed activity should have AI at its core, including its applications in scientific research and related disciplines. The proposed activity should demonstrate a meaningful impact on the applicant’s academic, research or professional development. The skills and competencies to be developed through the activity should be clearly identified. Timing and career development: Why is this activity particularly relevant at this stage of the applicant’s career? Why is now the right time to pursue it? Are there alternative funding opportunities available to the applicant? Knowledge sharing and alignment with WAI’s vision. Application The application process consists of two stages. For the pre-selection stage, applicants must complete the online form, providing all the information required to justify the requested budget and explain the purpose and expected impact of the proposed activity. Shortlisted applicants will then be invited to a 15 minute online interview (expected to take place in last week of January), consisting of a 5 minute presentation followed by 10 minutes of questions from the panel. To apply for a grant during the pre-selection stage, applicants must complete a brief online form and provide the following information: Requested amount: Up to £1,000, with a fully justified budget detailing the expected costs (e.g., conference registration fees, workshop fees, travel, and other expenses). If the maximum budget of £1,000 does not cover all the expenses for the activity, please justify how you will cover the remaining costs. Departmental account number (please enter your supervisor’s/mentor’s departmental F account number for the fund transfer). Purpose of the grant: A one-sentence summary of the proposed activity and its purpose. Brief proposal (up to 300 words), including: A clear description of the planned activity. The main motivation for participating in the activity. Expected impact on career development (up to 100 words), describing the anticipated learning outcomes and how the activity will contribute to your research and professional growth. Curriculum Vitae (CV) Click here to apply For more information, visit IX-WAI Early Career Development Grant . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article SAIS Livestock Investment Readiness Programme 2027 (up to €15,000) Next Article 15 Global Scholarship Opportunities Currently Open – November 5, 2026 Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 3 days Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 November 10, 2026 Closes in 24 days QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) November 9, 2026 Closes in 35 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
