      "pageTitle": "International Blue Carbon Institute (IBCI) Fellowship Program 2027 ($60,000 grant) &#8211; Opportunity Desk",
      "pageDescription": "",
      "evidenceText": "International Blue Carbon Institute (IBCI) Fellowship Program 2027 ($60,000 grant) – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram International Blue Carbon Institute (IBCI) Fellowship Program 2027 ($60,000 grant) Jude Ogar November 6, 2026 2 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: November 23, 2026 Applications for the International Blue Carbon Institute (IBCI) Fellowship Program 2027 are now open. The International Blue Carbon Institute (IBCI) Fellowship program advances the conservation, restoration, and protection of blue carbon ecosystems for their climate mitigation and adaptation benefits. The program is a cornerstone of the IBCI’s mission to scale global blue carbon action through innovative research, capacity building and collaboration to maximize climate impact. The goals of the fellowship are threefold: To advance blue carbon science and innovation in the implementation of blue carbon solutions To build capacity that contributes to the protection, restoration and conservation of blue carbon ecosystems To scale up blue carbon solutions through multi-disciplinary collaboration, knowledge building and sharing Grant Each fellow will receive a grant of USD $60,000 to support either new programs and projects or existing research endeavors. Supported activities may include supplementing current research projects, travel for laboratory studies, purchase of equipment, and other additional research costs (e.g., publication fees, field assistants). In addition to the grant, fellows may receive funding to attend annual International Blue Carbon Scientific Working Group meetings convened by the Blue Carbon Initiative and Conservation International. Eligibility Applications are welcome from all regions. To ensure geographic representation, they strongly encourage applications from researchers and practitioners working in the Global South, including but not limited to Africa, Latin America and the Caribbean, South and Southeast Asia, and the Pacific Islands. Applicants are encouraged to demonstrate how the work supported by the IBCI Fellowship will be impactful for on-the-ground activities and local communities in these regions. For this cycle, applications from Africa are particularly encouraged. The Fellowship welcomes applications across all blue carbon ecosystems, including mangroves, salt marshes, seagrasses and kelp forests. Application To apply for the IBCI Fellowship Program, submit your application here by uploading the following materials: Proof of employment/Letter of Support from your Institution Curriculum Vitae Completed IBCI Fellowship Application Form Completed Budget Sheet Click here to upload application to MicroSoft Onedrive For more information, visit IBCI Fellowship . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article Reagan-Fascell Democracy Fellows Program 2027-2028 (Fully-funded) Next Article Asia Foundation Development Fellows Program 2027 Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 3 days Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 80 days Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 21 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
