      "evidenceText": "Arewa Creative Writing and Advocacy Fellowship (ACWAF) 2026 – Cohort 1 – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram Arewa Creative Writing and Advocacy Fellowship (ACWAF) 2026 – Cohort 1 Jude Ogar November 7, 2026 1 Min Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: November 30, 2026 Applications are open for the Arewa Creative Writing and Advocacy Fellowship (ACWAF) 2026 . The Arewa Creative Writing and Advocacy Fellowship (ACWAF) is an initiative by the Poetic Wednesdays Initiative, supported by the Nigeria Youth Futures Fund (NYFF). For Cohort 1, this edition is open exclusively to emerging writers, storytellers, and spoken word artists from Northern Nigeria. The fellowship is a 6-8 week hybrid program designed to equip participants with skills in creative nonfiction, civic storytelling, policy framing, editorial ethics, fact-checking, and multimedia narrative techniques to advocate on governance, democracy, elections, voter rights, and youth rights. The physical aspect will be held in Kano State.  Benefits Hybrid training 1-on-1 mentorship Editorial/publication support Data stipends and direct networking opportunities Eligibility Open to emerging writers and aspiring advocates from Northern Nigeria. Should be available for the physical part of the program in Kano State. Application Click here to apply For more information, visit ACWAF . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article Call for judges : Join the OD Impact Challenge 2026 global judging panel Next Article How to Get a Scholarship with a Third-Class Degree: 7 Practical Steps to Improve Your Chances Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 3 days Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 80 days Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 21 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
