ve data journalism more accessible to readers. It covers numerous categories — geography, money, time, risk, etc. — and includes other tools and resource links, as well as a handy quiz to test yourself. GIJC27 UPDATES 2027 Global Shining Light Award Submissions Now Open This unique award honors investigative journalism in a developing or transitioning country, done under threat, duress, or dire conditions. Apply be Feb 28, 2027. Read More → MASTERCLASS VIDEOS Collaborating with Scientists, Protecting Against Legal Threats In GIJN Academy’s latest series of masterclass videos, French investigative reporter Stéphane Horel discusses how journalists can partner with experts and scientists to strengthen their investigations and Media Defense CEO Carlos Gaio offers practical advice for avoiding and mitigating legal attacks on your reporting . See More → Tips, Tools, & Opportunities Guide to Making FOI Requests in Europe This resource by Arena for Journalism in Europe informs journalists about how to make cross-border FOI requests. Investigating Data Centers Webinar A webinar by Pulitzer Center for journalists interested in researching data centers. Date: November 17. Hans Staiger Award For journalists in the OCCRP network to pursue an investigative project. Apply by November 15. German - Latin American Programme A program for young journalists from Latin America to work in Germany and vice versa. Apply by November 22. JournalismAI Strategy Lab – Africa A program for media professionals in Africa to learn about AI use in journalism. Apply by November 29. Stories of the Week Brazil: Anatomy of a Land Grab Mongabay lifted the lid on how a fast-tracked law and a social media blitz legitimized and encouraged around 500 people to invade the Ituna/Itatá Indigenous Territory. China/Zambia: China Capital ICIJ revealed that Chinese banking giants piled loans onto debt-ridden Zambia, then adopted a hardball stance when it came time for repayment. Colombia/Ecuador: Childhoods Captured Connectas and partners investigated the recruitment and exploitation of children and adolescents by armed and criminal structures in Colombia and Ecuador. Europe: Europe’s Data Center Exploitation An investigation by Investigate Europe and partners uncovered disturbing evidence of potential exploitation of workers building Europe’s data centers. Nepal: Felling Trees Without Compensation CIJ Nepal dug into the felling of trees, & how billions of Nepalese rupee went unpaid by the government to a forest development fund. View email in browser 2336 Wisconsin Ave NW, PO Box 32322, Washington DC, 20007 update your preferences or unsubscribe",
