      "pageDescription": "How Lorenzo Musetti won the 2026 ATP 250 in Lyon: 5 charts to understand it.",
      "evidenceText": "How Musetti won the ATP 250 in Lyon - Danilo De Rosa 1 Second serve 2 Placement 3 Return 4 Variation 5 Crosscourt backhand 59.7% of second-serve points won in the tournament (80/134), against 55% for his personal average and 51% for the Tour The second serve in Lyon was a weapon for Musetti. Despite a speed slightly below his personal average, over the five matches he won 59.7% of the points played on his second serve, almost five points above his 52-week average and almost nine above the Tour average. In every round he did better than his opponent on the same stat: the widest gap was against Arnaldi (56% to 32%), the narrowest against Cobolli (54% to 47%), and in the final he won 14 points out of 20, or 70%, against 47% for Fritz. Musetti's second serve outperformed his opponents' Percentage of points won on one's own second serve. Dashed lines are the 52-week averages Percentage of points won on a player's own second serve. Against Arnaldi: Musetti 56% (9/16), opponent 32% (8/25). Against Kouamé: Musetti 56% (10/18), opponent 42% (11/26). Against Van Assche: Musetti 63% (26/41), opponent 42% (18/43). Against Cobolli: Musetti 54% (21/39), opponent 47% (15/32). Against Fritz: Musetti 70% (14/20), opponent 47% (8/17). In the tournament Musetti won 60% (80/134); his 52-week average is 55% and the Tour average 51%. Data courtesy of TennisViz and Courtside Advantage Musetti's second serve outperformed his opponents' × Musetti's second serve outperformed his opponents' Match Musetti Opponent Round 1, Arnaldi 56% (9/16) 32% (8/25) Round 2, Kouamé 56% (10/18) 42% (11/26) Quarterfinal, Van Assche 63% (26/41) 42% (18/43) Semifinal, Cobolli 54% (21/39) 47% (15/32) Final, Fritz 70% (14/20) 47% (8/17) Points won on a player's own second serve, with the count in parentheses. 52-week averages. His average: 55%. Tour average: 51%.",
